  "note": "Triennial whole-council election of Lisburn Urban District Council (calendar polling day 18 May 1949); no poll: nominations on 4 May 1949 were 6 for Central, 5 for North and 3 for the 4 South Ward seats, all returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1949, p. 3); the retiring member Jas. M'Keown, who was not nominated, was deemed re-elected to the fourth South seat (Lisburn Standard, 6 May 1949, p. 4), and sat as a member at the council's June meeting (Lisburn Standard, 10 June 1949, p. 4). Returned unopposed.",
